{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאכילך את המן למען הודיעך", :translit "va'ya'akhil'kha et ha-man lema'an hodi'akha", :gloss "and He fed you the manna so that He might make you know"} {:he "ומנך נתת להם להשכילם", :translit "u-mannakha natata lahem le-haskilam", :gloss "and from You You gave them to make them understand"} {:he "לא ניתנה תורה אלא לאוכלי המן", :translit "lo nitnah torah ela le-okhlei ha-man", :gloss "the Torah was not given except to eaters of the manna"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse-level wordplay: הודיעך linked to להשכילם — both root ה-כ-ל / י-ד-ע convey knowledge granted through food"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that the Torah was given only to those who ate the manna (Shabbat 88a). The verse in Nehemiah 9:20 records that God gave manna and it is associated with imparting understanding.", :sources ["Shabbat 88a" "Nehemiah 9:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "על ה", :translit "al ha", :gloss "on the"} {:he "והקרבתם על הלחם", :translit "ve-hikravtem al ha-lekhem", :gloss "and you shall offer upon the bread"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["על ה" "והקרבתם על הלחם"]}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah states that sacrifices sustain the world (Pirkei Avot 1:2). The phrase על הלחם appears in the instructions for the shelamim offering in Leviticus 23:17.", :sources ["Pirkei Avot 1:2" "Leviticus 23:17"]}} {:quotes [{:he "יחיה האדם", :translit "yikhyeh ha-adam", :gloss "man lives"} {:he "שמלתך לא בלת'", :translit "sal'takha lo bal't", :gloss "your garment did not wear out"} {:he "שמלתך לא סלתה", :translit "sal'takha lo soletah", :gloss "your garment, not its flour"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verse Deut 8:4 is read as a continuation of Deut 8:3, connecting 'man lives' to 'your garment did not wear out'"} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: סלתה (wore out) reparsed as from סלת (fine flour), yielding 'not worn out / not flour'"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that the Israelites' garments grew with them and did not wear out during the forty years in the wilderness, derived as a fortiori from wheat: if the wheat-derived manna did not spoil, the garments certainly did not wear out (Shabbat 88b, Berakhot 57b, and parallels).", :sources ["Shabbat 88b" "Berakhot 57b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse-level wordplay: הודיעך linked to להשכילם — both root ה-כ-ל / י-ד-ע convey knowledge granted through food", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["על ה" "והקרבתם על הלחם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "על ה", :refs ["Genesis 42:36" "1 Kings 13:30" "Hosea 7:16"], :n 3, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "והקרבתם על הלחם", :refs ["Leviticus 23:18"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Adjacent verse Deut 8:4 is read as a continuation of Deut 8:3, connecting 'man lives' to 'your garment did not wear out'", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: סלתה (wore out) reparsed as from סלת (fine flour), yielding 'not worn out / not flour'", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:17.838948577Z", :model "glm-5.2"}